    {
      "template_id": "text",
      "color_scheme": "light",
      "content": {
        "text_elements": [
          {
            "template_id": "paragraph_medium",
            "content": {
              "text": "The energy sector emissions include <a href=\"https://www.wri.org/insights/4-charts-explain-greenhouse-gas-emissions-countries-and-sectors\"><u>electricity and heat generation (29.7%), transportation (13.7%), manufacturing and construction (12.7%), and buildings (6.6%)</u></a>. Fugitive emissions (those released during fossil fuel production or transmission) and emissions from other fuel combustion are also significant contributors.<br /> <br />Residential buildings represent the largest share of energy sector emissions, <a href=\"https://www.wri.org/insights/4-charts-explain-greenhouse-gas-emissions-countries-and-sectors\"><u>contributing 12.5% to global emissions</u></a>. This includes emissions from electricity generation for household use and direct fossil fuel consumption, such as cooking with gas. Road transportation is another major source, accounting for <a href=\"https://www.wri.org/insights/4-charts-explain-greenhouse-gas-emissions-countries-and-sectors\"><u>12.2% of global emissions</u></a>."
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
